WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.990
- Do you remember the first time

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:03.150
you ever performed anywhere,
like when you were a kid?

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.580
- Yeah, I remember the
first time singing live.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.580
I had this teacher at
school called Mr. Wren,

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.990
and I idolized him

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.900
and I wanted to be like him.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.190
He was the kind of teacher

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.960
that all the guy teachers wanted to be

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.330
and all the girl teachers
wanted to be with,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.524
that kind of guy, you know.

00:00:19.524 --> 00:00:22.470
If we're lucky in our lives,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.760
we all have that one person that sees us.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:25.640
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.590
- And he saw me and he sang

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.270
and I wanted to be just like him.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.920
So he would--
- That's so cool.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.420
- So I started singing.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.710
Then he would encourage me to sing

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.710
and he'd put me on stage to
sing a song by Johnny Nash

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.360
at the Parents and Teachers
Association evening.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.600
Now, my parents had never
heard me sing before.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.570
They didn't even know that I sang.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.607
And I remember him calling
my name to the stage, he said

00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:53.850
"And now, we're gonna have Young Seal

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.280
and he's gonna sing
this Johnny Nash song."

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.760
I can see clearly.
- Yeah.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.760
♪ I can see clearly
now, the rain is gone ♪

00:01:02.887 --> 00:01:05.867
♪ It's gonna be a bright, bright ♪

00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:07.800
♪ Sunshiney day ♪

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.060
- Such a great song.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:09.893
Yeah.

00:01:09.893 --> 00:01:10.968
- So he goes.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.540
- Feel free to do that at any
moment during this interview.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.100
It sounds so sexy.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.540
It's so cool.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.343
It is, your rasp, I like.

00:01:18.604 --> 00:01:21.300
You know what it is, when I'm
tired, like I'm tired today,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.340
but when I'm tired, I love
singing when I'm tired

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.410
'cause I feel like I
can sound cool like you

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.940
or I'm like maybe Tony Braxton.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.396
You have that low raspy just like, mm.

00:01:29.396 --> 00:01:31.170
I don't have that most of the time.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.003
Keep going, so sorry.

00:01:32.003 --> 00:01:33.990
How did you do with the
song when you were a kid?

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.040
Were you nervous on the stage then?

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.120
- Well, yeah, I was.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.530
I remember him calling me

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.450
and it's like that scene in a movie

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.430
where everything goes silent

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.170
and you can hear a pin drop.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.003
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.090
- And 'cause it was acapella

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.520
and no one had ever heard me
sing before, so I remember.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.284
- You didn't even sing with
music for the first time?

00:01:49.284 --> 00:01:50.130
- No, no.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.140
It was just.
- [Kelly] Bold.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.930
- So he called me on stage
and I remember standing there

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:58.350
and looking out, and seeing
everyone in the audience

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.460
just pretty much like I'm seeing you

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.604
except there were more of you.

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:06.604
And I just, I wanted
the stage to just open

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.210
and swallow me up, you know?

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.435
- [Kelly] So nervous.

00:02:10.435 --> 00:02:11.268
- It was the last place I wanted to be,

00:02:11.268 --> 00:02:12.780
and I was kind of like I was frozen,

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.890
but somehow I closed my
eyes and got through it,

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:21.890
and sang, and kept my eyes
closed at the end of it.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.820
And then just everyone applauded,

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.825
and I remember looking up
and seeing my parents going.

00:02:25.825 --> 00:02:28.200
- Like "What?"

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:33.120
- And the interesting
thing about that experience

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.250
is that that place, that stage

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.240
that felt like the most terrifying,

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.420
most lonely place all of
a sudden felt like home.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.370
And I never forgot that feeling.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.650
So, I guess throughout my life,

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.200
I did different things
until I eventually decided

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.730
I was gonna commit to singing.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.680
But I never forgot that feeling.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.272
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:54.272 --> 00:02:55.128
- And I always knew that
I would come back to that.

00:02:55.128 --> 00:02:58.110
- I love that story, but I
also love that you pointed out

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.560
it is like, if one person
sees you when you're younger

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.210
and it gives you confidence

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.430
like that you can do something
and maybe you're special

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.571
and every kid likes to
feel special, right?

00:03:07.571 --> 00:03:08.404
- Yeah, of course.

00:03:08.404 --> 00:03:10.560
- It does take one person,
I think to like, I mean,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.640
it's good if it's more than one,

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.230
but if it's just one, that's nice

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.050
that you feel like you
maybe found something

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.700
that you're special at and it gives that,

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.533
that's what happened to me too.

00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:21.210
- And it really, and you
are absolutely right.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.560
- It changes your personality, everything.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.650
- Yeah, it really comes
down to who, you know,

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:28.200
that champion or those
champions in your life

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.570
that do see you and
encourage you to be special.

00:03:35.121 --> 00:03:35.954
- Yeah.

00:03:35.954 --> 00:03:37.260
- And who knows, if not for Mr. Wren,

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.410
perhaps, you know, it
wouldn't have happened for me.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.810
I certainly wouldn't
have had that experience.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.160
And throughout my life,

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.930
I've had timely people who
have come and championed me

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.240
and have seen me in different ways

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.330
and given me the inspiration
and the courage to move on,

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.840
which is why I feel so
strongly about mentoring.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:58.673
- Yeah.

00:04:01.486 --> 00:04:03.510
- I found out fairly recently

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.360
that as much as I love singing

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.980
and as much as I love performing

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:12.980
and as much as music is a part of my life,

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.330
I really love coaching.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:18.810
I really love, I would much rather

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.180
see somebody else transcend
- Yeah.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.750
- Whatever's holding them
back than doing it myself.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.102
I get more pleasure out of that.

00:04:27.102 --> 00:04:30.150
- That's why I love being
a part of "The Voice."

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.770
Yeah, 'cause it's like everybody

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.320
and especially 'cause I
came from that environment,

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.720
like it's the most awesome
thing to be blessed

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.553
in your career.

00:04:37.553 --> 00:04:39.960
A lot of people can sing, a lot
of people can do what we do.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.220
Don't have your tone, but like, you know,

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.510
a lot of people can do what we do,

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.600
and it's cool to be able to
like look at someone younger

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.060
and go, "Let me show you
what maybe you're not seeing,

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:48.893
that little light in you."

00:04:48.893 --> 00:04:50.610
And it's so cool to be able
to bring that out of people.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.233
It is so gratifying.

